We need answer JSON only. Need assess citation. FastUMI sentence: "Various control interfaces, including AR controllers [31, 8], haptic controllers [29, 13], 3D spacemouses [27], and newly explored leader-follower systems [42] are developed to build teleoperated systems." Reference [31] is DexHub and DART paper. It is about AR teleoperation platform using Apple Vision Pro, hand tracking, cloud simulation. Does it support claim that AR controllers are developed to build teleoperated systems? Yes, DART is an AR-based teleoperation system/controller. Need quote verbatim from cited paper max 60 words. Need exact passage. Could use abstract: "We introduce DART, a teleoperation plat- form designed for crowdsourcing that reimagines robotic data collection by leveraging cloud-based simulation and augmented reality (AR) to address many limitations of prior data collection efforts." But line break hyphen "plat- form" in text. Need copy exactly character for character from provided text. Better choose a clean sentence without hyphenation: "To that end, we introduce DART, a Dexterous Augmented Reality Teleoperation system, enabling anyone in the world to teleoperate robots in simulation with an intuitive, game- like AR interface." Contains "game- like" hyphen line break. Could still copy exactly. Or "DART’s high-fidelity AR rendering allows users to observe the scene in great detail with minimal occlusion, enabling teleoperation of complex tasks." This supports AR controller? It mentions AR rendering, not controller. Better: "We introduce DART, a teleoperation plat- form designed for crowdsourcing that reimagines robotic data collection by leveraging cloud-based simulation and augmented reality (AR) to address many limitations of prior data collection efforts." It has hyphenation due line break. We can copy exactly as in text: "We introduce DART, a teleoperation plat- form designed for crowdsourcing that reimagines robotic data collection by leveraging cloud-based simulation and augmented reality (AR) to address many limitations of prior data collection efforts." That's 33 words? Let's count: We1 introduce2 DART,3 a4 teleoperation5 plat-6 form7 designed8 for9 crowdsourcing10 that11 reimagines12 robotic13 data14 collection15 by16 leveraging17 cloud-based18 simulation19 and20 augmented21 reality22 (AR)23 to24 address25 many26 limitations27 of28 prior29 data30 collection31 efforts32. Good. But "plat- form" is awkward but exact. Alternatively from Fig 1: "We present DART, Dexterous Augmented Reality Teleoperation system, enabling intuitive, low-latency teleoperation with cloud-hosted simulation." This is clean and directly supports AR teleoperation. It's in figure caption. Quote: "We present DART, Dexterous Augmented Reality Teleoperation system, enabling intuitive, low-latency teleoperation with cloud-hosted simulation." 16 words. Good. Use that.

Need claim one sentence: FastUMI relies on [31] as an example of an AR controller/interface developed for teleoperated systems. Status supported. Reason: The cited paper presents DART, an AR-based teleoperation system, so it backs the claim. Need include reason even for supported? Schema says reason required for incorrect or unverifiable, but can include anyway. We'll include concise reason.

Need ensure JSON valid, no extra text. Quote exactly from cited text. Check exact caption: "Fig. 1: We present DART, Dexterous Augmented Reality Teleoperation system, enabling intuitive, low-latency teleoperation with cloud-hosted simulation." The quote should be verbatim passage, can omit "Fig. 1:"? It says copy quote exactly from cited text. If we include substring starting "We present..." that's exact. Good.

Need final only JSON object.
